APIs - Application Programmable Interfaces- Set of rules that determine how two software systems can communicate with each other and share information.
Workflow: Client sends a request to an API which fetches the corresponding relevant data from API Server and delivers it to the client as a response 
(Eg- Customer- waiter- API server)

API Request- Endpoint (URL the provides access to a specific resource)
             Method (Type of operations that the client would like to perform on the given resource)
             Parameters (Variables with specific instructions for the request)
             Request headers (Additional details regarding the request)
             Request body (Actual Data) 

API Response- Consist of status code, response headers and response body. 

Types- (Categorized by their architectural style)
REST
SOAP
GraphQL
Webhooks
gRPC 

How API parameters work-URL and Endpoints-

Query paramters-(?key=value)  ---> used for filtering 
Eg- GET /products?category=shoes&limit=10

Path parameters-(/resource/:id) ----> used for identity
Eg- GET /USERS/123 

Header Parameters- Carry metadata that shapes how requests are processed and how the responses are interpreted.
Eg: This is a handler: app.post('/orders', (req, res) => { const contentType = req.get('Content-Type'); // e.g., application/json const accept = req.get('Accept'); // e.g., application/json const auth = req.get('Authorization'); // e.g., Bearer <token> const ua = req.get('User-Agent'); // validate headers, then handle request... res.set('Content-Type', 'application/json'); // declare response type return res.json({ ok: true, contentType, accept, ua, hasAuth: Boolean(auth) }); });

Content Negotiation: Negotiation regarding the compatible content type; when a client wants a resource , thr client requests it via a URL. The server uses this URL to choose one of the variants of the responses. 
There are several types of negotiations-
              Server-driven content negotiation- server uses internal algo to choose what resposne to send.(not scalable as there is one header per feature)
              Agent-driven negotiation- Server sends back a page that has multiple links to alternate resouces  when faced with an ambiguous request 
              

